        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ames–Florida House, New York, Quebec, United States city\n- Concepts: Deicke bentonite, Millbrig bentonite, Ordovician ash beds\n\nFacts:\n- Ames–Florida House was built in 1856.\n- Ames–Florida House is in a United States city located between New York and Quebec, Canada.\n- The referenced United States city was the most affected during the era in which the Deicke and Millbrig bentonite layers were formed.\n- Deicke bentonite and Millbrig bentonite are bentonite layers formed from Ordovician volcanic ash deposits.",
